# What this repository is, as far as a forge is concerned.
#
# `vendor/` is 379,332 lines against MCF's own 79,000, and it is committed
# deliberately: `.cargo/config.toml` replaces the registry with it so that
# every build is offline and no dependency is resolved at build time (B-322,
# §3.12). Left unmarked, a forge attributes all of it to this project and
# reports MCF as a cryptography library.
#
# `linguist-vendored` keeps it out of the language statistics and collapses it
# in diffs by default. It changes nothing about the build: the tree is still
# there and still what cargo reads.
vendor/** linguist-vendored

# The documents are the project rather than an accompaniment to it — the rules
# are enforced, the findings are evidence, and the register is what the work is
# tracked in. They are marked as documentation so that a forge counts them as
# what they are, and `linguist-detectable` so they are still counted at all.
doc/** linguist-documentation
doc/** linguist-detectable

# Text is normalised on the way in and checked out with the platform's endings.
# MCF runs on Linux, and a contributor reading it on another platform should
# not see the whole tree as modified.
* text=auto eol=lf
